<% content_for :title, "Design System" %>

<div class="h-screen overflow-y-auto">
<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-10 space-y-12">
  <header>
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Design system</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-1">
      Every reusable piece of UI in this app, rendered live from the same helpers and partials the
      real views call — <%= link_to "back to the app", root_path, class: "text-indigo-600 hover:underline" %>.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="space-y-3">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800">Buttons</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
      <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded">ds_button(variant)</code> in
      <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded">app/helpers/design_system_helper.rb</code>. Use on
      <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded">f.submit</code>, <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded">link_to</code>
      or <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded">button_to</code> — never retype the Tailwind classes by hand.
    </p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 p-4 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg bg-white">
      <button type="button" class="<%= ds_button(:primary) %>">Primary</button>
      <button type="button" class="<%= ds_button(:dark) %>">Dark</button>
      <button type="button" class="<%= ds_button(:danger) %>">Danger</button>
      <button type="button" class="<%= ds_button(:danger_text) %>">Danger (text)</button>
      <button type="button" class="<%= ds_button(:ghost) %>">Ghost</button>
      <button type="button" class="<%= ds_button(:milestone) %>">Milestone</button>
      <button type="button" class="<%= ds_button(:task) %>">Task</button>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-gray-400">
      Primary = the default save/confirm action inside an overlay. Dark = the one primary create
      action on the main screen ("+ Project"). Danger / danger (text) = destructive actions, solid
      or as an inline link. Ghost = a low-emphasis secondary action. Milestone / task match the
      amber ◆ / blue ▬ color coding used everywhere else, for their own "Add" buttons.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800">Form fields</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
      Border, padding, radius and focus ring come from a <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded">@layer base</code>
      rule in <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded">app/assets/tailwind/application.css</code> — every
      text/date/number/textarea gets this automatically. Pass
      <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded">class: ds_field</code> (nothing) for the default full-width
      field, or <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded">class: ds_field(width: "w-1/2")</code> for a
      side-by-side pair.
    </p>
    <div class="p-4 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg bg-white space-y-3 max-w-sm">
      <input type="text" placeholder="Full-width text field" class="<%= ds_field %>">
      <div class="flex gap-2">
        <input type="date" class="<%= ds_field(width: "w-1/2") %>">
        <input type="date" class="<%= ds_field(width: "w-1/2") %>">
      </div>
      <textarea placeholder="Notes (optional)" rows="2" class="<%= ds_field %>"></textarea>
      <label class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-gray-700">
        <input type="checkbox"> A checkbox, for confirmation-style forms
      </label>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800">Alerts</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
      <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded">ds_alert(:error)</code> /
      <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded">ds_alert(:success)</code> — used for both real flash
      messages and inline warnings (e.g. the import overlay's destructive-action notice).
    </p>
    <div class="space-y-2">
      <p class="<%= ds_alert(:error) %>">Something needs your attention.</p>
      <p class="<%= ds_alert(:success) %>">Saved successfully.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800">Section label</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500"><code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded">ds_section_label</code> — the small uppercase heading used inside overlays ("Milestones & tasks", "Work in this sprint", …).</p>
    <div class="p-4 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg bg-white">
      <h4 class="<%= ds_section_label %>">Example section</h4>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800">Modal header</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">
      <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded">render "shared/modal_header", title: "…"</code> — every
      overlay (project card, milestone/task detail, sprint config, import) opens with this. Pass a
      plain string, or <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded">safe_join([tag.span("◆", class: "text-amber-500"), name], " ")</code>
      for a title with an icon.
    </p>
    <div class="p-4 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg bg-white max-w-sm">
      <%= render "shared/modal_header", title: safe_join([ tag.span("◆", class: "text-amber-500"), "Example overlay" ], " ") %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800">Row type indicators</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">Used on the Gantt chart's label column and everywhere a milestone/task is listed by name.</p>
    <div class="p-4 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg bg-white flex flex-col gap-2 text-sm text-gray-700">
      <span><span class="text-amber-500">◆</span> Milestone — a single date</span>
      <span><span class="text-blue-500">▬</span> Task — a date range</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-3">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800">Sprint badge</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">From the Sprints configuration list.</p>
    <div class="p-4 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg bg-white flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <span class="text-xs font-medium text-emerald-700 bg-emerald-50 px-2 py-1 rounded flex items-center gap-1">
        <span class="text-emerald-600">&#9679;</span> Current sprint
      </span>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
</div>
